Thalheimer answers every critic in print, at length, with footnotes. Fewer comrades read him than should, but those who do argue better for it.

@transitional
title: Argue for Transitional Demands
subtitle: Workers' control of production, seizure of real values. Workers listen; the Left calls it reformism.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 4; last_advisor_action = 1; worker_support += 4; spd_relation += 3; offensive_satisfaction -= 5; unionist_satisfaction += 4; lean_unionist += 2

Not the dictatorship of the proletariat tomorrow, Thalheimer writes, but demands that lead towards it: control of the factories, taxes on the propertied, bread for the unemployed.
